  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased capacity of labour administration and social partners on workplace compliance and better working conditions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO will continue assisting the Government in development of the national OSH profile and prevention of violation of fundamental rights at work. The initiative includes increasing capacity of labour inspectors and strengthening enforcement and compliance mechanisms. Following the recent amendments to the Labour Code, the ILO will provide policy and capacity building support to the tripartite constituents on   prevention of violence and harassment in the world of work. Additionally, the ILO promotes decent work in the care economy through capacity building, awareness raising, and evidence-based reports on investing in care services and decent working conditions of care workers including domestic workers and community-based care workers in collaboration with UN Women and WHO for policy recommendations. The tripartite dialogue on the country assessment on care work prepared by using the ILO Global Tool on Care Policy Investment on Simulator will be facilitated.</narrative>
  </description>
